Level 14 password: For this level there isn't actually a flag that represents the password. In order to login to level 14 you have to ssh using a private key.

*Post note: the password for level 14 is stored in /etc/bandit_pass/bandit14. The permissions are enabled for bandit14 to see, which we use for the next level*

Notes:
- Used scp to securely copy the private ssh key from the bandit13 account onto my local computer.
- Opened the local computer current working directory to check that the file was copied properly
- Changed the permissions of the private key so that the owner (me) can read and write it
- Used the private ssh key to log in to bandit14 

Commands used in localhost (not bandit server):

``` Shell
 1013  scp -P 2220 bandit13@bandit.labs.overthewire.org:/home/bandit13/sshkey.private .

 1014  open .

 1015  chmod 600 ./sshkey.private

 1016  ssh -i ./sshkey.private bandit14@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
```

